        {"after": "# Greenhouse effect, global warming, climate change",
         "md": "The **greenhouse effect** is natural and life-giving: CO2, CH4, water vapour and other gases let sunlight in but slow the infrared escape, keeping Earth ~33°C warmer than it would be. The problem is the **enhanced** effect: fossil fuel burning and deforestation have raised CO2 from ~280 to over 420 ppm, driving **global warming** and with it **climate change** — shifting rainfall, melting ice, rising seas."},
